# Design: boolean --remote plus --hub-addr on ohya mcp

## Problem
README.md printed `ohya mcp --remote` bare (Use block and the Claude
Code registration) but --remote was a string flag with an empty
default, so the bare form exited at "flag needs an argument: -remote".

## Why This Way
Go's flag package always requires a value for a string flag, even one
with a non-empty default — giving --remote the documented default
address alone could never make the bare form parse. Only a boolean
flag parses without an argument, so --remote selects remote mode and
the address moves to --hub-addr with the tailcat.DefaultHubAddr()
default. --hub-addr deliberately reuses join's flag name, default,
and usage text so both commands share one vocabulary for the same
concept.

## Alternatives Considered
- **String --remote with default address**: cannot parse bare — the
  failure the README printed; rejected.
- **Custom flag.Value with IsBoolFlag() accepting both "true" and an
  address**: the space-separated address form would become a
  positional argument; surprising behavior for no gain; rejected.

## Gotchas
- `--remote <address>` (old form) now fails as "unexpected argument"
  rather than parsing; pre-MVP, the README is the contract.

